the international geneva motor show was  one of the biggest dates on the european  and global car calendar it plays host to  some seven hundred thousand visitors  this year fans can look forward to over  130 new models and concept cars  we were there to cover the highlights  and new developments  volkswagen presents the new terran  while the first generation was based on  the caddies platform this edition is  built around vw's mqb modular  architecture the second generation  terran is lighter but 10 centimeters  longer  the new terran has a completely  different basis from its predecessor  explains volkswagen's group ceo martin  vintercorn but it's still geared to its  customers from families with children to  sports enthusiasts he's confident vw has  hit the bull's eye  the bmw 2-series grand active tour is 21  centimeters longer and five centimeters  taller than its little brother the  regular grand tour  it's also available with all-wheel drive  a third row of seats gives the grand  active tour room for seven  the second row can be slid 13  centimeters back and forth  the new mpv will hit showroom floors in  june  this is more than just a long version of  the active tour says bmw's peter henry  the two may be related but this is an  independent concept with which bmw wants  to reach new target groups  the porsche stand is obviously a  distinctly sporty affair debuting in  geneva is a gt edition of the cayman it  incorporates parts from the 911 gt3 a  283 kilowatt 3.8 liter boxer engine lets  the cayman gt4 post a lap time of 7  minutes and 40 seconds for the legendary  north loop of the nurburgring track  ceo matias mula is proud to present two  very sporty models there's the gt3 rs  and the gt4 the flagship of the cayman  range  the duo further underlined porsche's  performance credentials these are  essentially street legal race cars he  the says smart includes twinamic a dual  clutch transmission making its debut in  geneva  packing a 52 kilowatt three-cylinder  engine it accelerates to 100 kilometers  per hour in 15.1 seconds  top speed is 151  fuel consumption is rated at 4.1 liters  for 100 kilometers  the 4-door 4-4 edition will feature the  new transmission later in the year  449 kilowatts from a v10 mid engine  makes the r8 v10 plus a certified  galloping gas guzzler it takes just 3.2  seconds to reach 100 kilometers per hour  top speed is 330 kilometers per hour the  r8 e-tron can only hit 250 kilometers  per hour but it is after all an  all-electric car a sports car for the  future  ceo rupert stadler calls the performance  sensational 600 or 610 horsepower is  outstanding  zero to 100 and 3.2 seconds is not bad  he reckons  the rh design makes it an ambassador for  the brand it boosts our image and taking  it to the next generation was a good  idea  toyota was in geneva to pull the wraps  off a freshened up version of the  avensis  the family car now comes with a  seriously modified front new safety  features and a new range of engines  it was developed in belgium designed in  france and built in britain  also raring to go a new iris in addition  to the classic combustion engines toyota  also offers an environmentally friendly  plug-in hybrid version the new iris hits  showrooms in the fall  lexus is wowing the crowds with the lfsa  an exciting new ultra compact study  measuring just three meters 45 it looks  custom-made for those congested city  streets but the two plus two cedar has  plenty of space for luxury too it's  unclear whether the lfsa will actually  become a production model  skoda caused something of a commotion  with the third generation superb  boasting luxury features and design plus  slick new colors  the trunk can hold  1276 leaders while neat ideas such as  two umbrellas in the front doors as well  as a lane assist and blind spot detect  system round off the package the new  skoda superb also comes in a four by  four version  seyat presents the leon st cupra great  utility value but also a real racer like  the compact version the st comes with a  choice of engines from 195 to 206  kilowatts  the more powerful version makes the  sprint to 100 kilometers per hour in a  six seconds flat  prices in germany start at 32 and a half  thousand euros  executives fancy an extra luxurious ride  will in future have the option of the  mercedes mybach pullman some six and a  half meters long it cuts a very stately  figure the rear compartment can  accommodate four people who can sit  facing each other  the s-600 pullman has a 50-year-old  heritage explains mercedes hola calenos  a car for heads of state kings and  queens and of course celebrities  6.5 meters long with a wheelbase of 3  meters 70 mean an unrivaled seating  comfort and in the back it's among the  quietest production car rides on the  road  following the atom model named after  opel's founder the carmaker's newest  model bears the name of his oldest son  carl it's smaller than the urban  lifestyle oriented atom but does seat up  to five people starting at nine and a  half thousand euros in germany the carl  is opal's new entry-level model  no carmaker's range seems complete these  days without a compact suv  the cx-3 is mazda's latest contribution  to the segment design and engineering  are as you would expect from mazda fuel  efficient engines will also help to  boost demand for the cx-3 in the  ever-expanding suv market  you
 

